build: 2026-06-23 v10.52.0 (Colorimetric CIE-1931 spectral colour — physically faithful sound→light, unified across screen + donut + immersive shader)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
notes: Answers the founder's physical-correctness question ("Die spectral sound Übersetzung … optisch physikalisch korrekt assoziiert?"). The spectral sound→light translation is now genuinely colorimetric and consistent everywhere. Replaced the old Bruton piecewise wavelength→RGB ("looks-right" approximation) with the CIE 1931 colour-matching functions (Wyman/Sloan/Shirley 2013 analytic multi-lobe Gaussian fit) → XYZ → linear sRGB (D65), gamut-clamped — hue is now physically faithful, brightness left to the audio level (per-channel normalize keeps full chroma so loudness, not eye-sensitivity, drives intensity). The EXACT same fit is mirrored in the Metal shader (MetalBioView.wavelengthToRGB) so the immersive visual and the spectral donut agree for the same frequency. Added SpectralColor.visibleWavelength(forToneHz:) — the genuine octave-transposition physics (f·2ⁿ into the visible band, λ=c/f), documented as the artistic "spectral/physical" mode (the 2ⁿ trick is convention, not a claim a note "is" a colour). Pitch-class→OKLCH hue stays the perceptual default for notes/chords/light (chord colours must mix perceptually, not blow out). Tests ungated so ci.yml executes them on Linux: non-negative XYZ, in-gamut 380–780 nm, correct dominant channel for red/green/blue/yellow, octave-equivalent tone→wavelength. Both gates green (xcode-compile-check validates the Metal shader; ci.yml runs SpectralColorCIETests).
